\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My heart is full of Christ, and longs
\par Its glorious matter to declare !
\par Of Him I make my loftier songs,
\par I cannot from His praise forbear ;
\par My ready tongue makes haste to sing
\par The glorious of my heavenly King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Fairer than all the earth-born race,
\par Perfect in comeliness Thou art ;
\par Replenished are Thy lips with grace,
\par And full of love Thy tender heart
\par God ever blest! we bow the knee,
\par And own all fullness dwells in Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Gird on Thy thigh the Spirit's sword,
\par And take to Thee Thy power divine ;
\par Stir up Thy strength, almighty Lord,
\par All power and majesty are Thine;
\par Assert Thy worship and renown ;
\par O all-redeeming God, come down !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come, and maintain Thy righteous cause,
\par And let Thy glorious toil succeed ;
\par Dispread the victory of Thy Cross,
\par Ride on, and prosper in Thy dead ;
\par Through earth triumphantly ride on,
\par And reign in every heart alone.\tab 
\par                                         Amen.\i 
\par \pard\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

